# Every dotenv file, at every depth — not just the two at the root.
#
# A .dockerignore pattern is matched against the path from the build context
# root, so a bare `.env.local` excluded the repository's own and nothing else.
# `apps/web/.env.local` is git-ignored, so it is a developer's private file that
# no reviewer ever sees — and `next build` reads it from the app directory and
# INLINES what it finds. One developer's `NEXT_PUBLIC_ALPPY_MOCK=1` therefore
# shipped inside the production image: every screen rendered the invented
# fixtures, the browser never called the API at all, and the middleware's
# session gate was dead-code-eliminated behind `MOCK === '1'`, so a visitor with
# no cookie got the whole authenticated shell. `docker compose up` looked
# perfect and was serving a demo.
#
# Nothing in either image legitimately wants a machine's local environment:
# configuration arrives as build args (apps/web/Dockerfile) and as the compose
# environment (apps/api).
.env
**/.env
**/.env.*
